    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2+y^2=a^2$.",
      "worked": "For $a\\ne0$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{x}{a},\\qquad \\sin\\theta=\\frac{y}{a}\\\\\n\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta&=1\\\\\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{a^2}&=1\\\\\nx^2+y^2&=a^2.\n\\end{aligned}$$\nIf $a=0$, then $x=y=0$, so the relation also holds.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
